<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρά̄-χολος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρᾱ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>quick to anger irascible</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				411c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.44
			</span></i> O., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύων ἀ.</span>
			<i>ill-tempered</i> dog, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				594a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλισσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epin.
					1.7
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχέρδου τῆς
			ἀκραχολωτάτης</span>, of a <i>spinous</i> pear. <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				164
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρόχολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1126a18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.268
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.604b
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			generally, <i>in passionate distress</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				24.61
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρᾱ-</span> is confirmed by
			metre of Com., 
				Ion.
			 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρη-</span>, and etym.
			(shortened fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρᾱτ-</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-</span> is freq. v.l. in
			codd. of early authors, as <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> l. c.)</div>
